    "text": "In R, you only need to install packages into your library once…(until you update R, then packages may need to be re-installed). To install a new package that you have not yet installed, use the install.packages(\"package_name\") function. You can run this line of code in your console (not in the script) to install any packages you don’t have yet.\nFor example, you may need to run install.packages(\"ggsci\") to install the ggsci package. That is required for this script."
